5851	<div class="sk-bx sk-talk" style="text-align:center"><h3>End of Chapter 1: "Dandelion Isle"</h3><p>The wind trapped under the Great Heron's wings broke free and seeped down beneath the island.</p><p>Dandelion Isle sinks no more. But the reason the great wind stopped still lies beyond — in the Rusty Windmill Isles.</p><p style="font-size:13px;color:#8a7458">⟨0⟩ Lv ⟨1⟩ · Murklings defeated ⟨2⟩ · Played ⟨3⟩ min<br>Cross to Chapter 2, the Rusty Windmill Isles, from the "Windways" at the Pinwheel Beacon (travel).</p><button class="sk-b p" data-a="x">Keep exploring</button></div>
5852	<div class="sk-bx sk-talk" style="text-align:center"><h3>End of Chapter 1, Part 1: "Dandelion Isle"</h3><p>The pinwheel began to turn again. Very faintly, but it's definitely wind.</p><p>But far off, over Nest Isle, the shadow of huge wings cut through the clouds…</p><p style="font-size:13px;color:#8a7458">⟨0⟩ Lv ⟨1⟩ · Murklings defeated ⟨2⟩ · Played ⟨3⟩ min<br>Talk to Chief Deulme again to continue Chapter 1, Part 2 (Reed Marsh and Nest Isle).</p><button class="sk-b p" data-a="x">Keep exploring</button></div>
